    "@value" : "S.V.Ilango"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@value" : "Planned Elapsed time (in ISO 8601 format) relative to a planned reference (CLTPTREF). This variable is useful where there are repetitive measures. Not a clock time or a date time variable. Represented as an ISO 8601 duration. Examples: -PT15M to represent the period of 15 minutes prior to the reference point indicated by CLTPTREF, or PT8H to represent the period of 8 hours after the reference point indicated by CLTPTREF."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C83083"
